  "worked_solution": "First, let's solve for the missing values:\n\n- When $P≡\\text{T}$ and $Q≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(P∧Q)∨¬P & ≡¬(\\text{T}∧\\text{T})∨¬\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡¬\\text{T}∨\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $P≡\\text{T}$ and $Q≡\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬P∨¬(Q∨P) & ≡¬\\text{T}∨¬(\\text{F}∨\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨¬\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $P≡\\text{F}$ and $Q≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(P∧Q)∨¬P & ≡¬(\\text{F}∧\\text{T})∨¬\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡¬\\text{F}∨\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∨\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur completed table is shown below.\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬P∨¬(Q∨P)\\,$ | $\\,¬(P∧Q)∨¬P\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nTo determine whether $¬P∨¬(Q∨P)$ is logically equivalent to $¬(P∧Q)∨¬P,$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.\n\nLooking at the last two columns, we see that they differ in the second row. Therefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n¬P∨¬(Q∨P)≢¬(P∧Q)∨¬P.\n$$",
